{{also|levant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|levant||[[rising]], sun's point of rising}}, form of {{m|fr|lever||to rise}}, from {{der|en|la|levō||to rise}} (cf. also the present participle {{m|la|levans}}), from {{m|la|levis||light, not heavy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈlɛv.ənt/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ləˈvænt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ænt|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The countries bordering the eastern [[Mediterranean Sea]], namely [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Palestine]], [[Jordan]] and [[Cyprus]] (and sometimes, especially in a historical context, also including [[Turkey]] and [[Egypt]], then part of the [[Ottoman Empire]]).
#: {{ant|en|Maghreb}} <!-- western Mediterranean, literally “where the sun sets” -->
# An [[easterly]] wind, generally in the western Mediterranean Sea
#: {{syn|en|levanter}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Levantine}}

